 with the  film i think it was a quieter  western than than most people would have  imagined  i think a great score goes in and out of  basically being in the front of your  thinking or your perception  certainly it seems to be music driven in  other parts of the movie it can be  quietly working on you  and you're not aware of it film music is  so wide open it can be anything the only  qualifications is that it's music in a  film you know  so film music music film  music has changed clearly you know every  generation the music  completely changes you know my wife and  my kids they call me a nerd i don't care  i'll take it  you know because when i'm not working on  a film  i'm learning i'm trying to figure out  how does this plug-in work how does this  synth work how do i manipulate it to do  what i needed to do  look it's just a matter of constantly  trying to up your game i see electronic  music and electronic scores as part of  the  essential palette now that every  composer needs to be able to  work with you know that's that's just  the way that's progress but i do hope  that  foundationally speaking orchestral music  stays part of the conversation whether  you're using an orchestra or a  synthesizer  or a guitar or a piano you know whatever  it may be  the emotional connection and the  spiritual connection with the film to  the music  that's that that will transcend  everything else  you

